      "message": "I don\u0027t think those would be different between archs? I think this could be solved in the gen_utils where you only make `args` and `response_file_content` arch-specific.\n\nMy point is that I don\u0027t think that `out`, `genrule_headers`, `srcs` and `tool_files` will ever be arch-specific. Specially `srcs`, `tool_files` and `genrule_headers`. I don\u0027t really care if a genrule uses more than it needs. `out` might be a problem but I hardly think that there\u0027s a genrule which have different `out` depending on arch.\n\nSo I think you could go back go `gn_utils` and generate only a single Target instead of `__arch` and you wouldn\u0027t need to merge them here.",
